# .gitignore — ESS-BMS-16S (public repository)
# Rule of thumb: commit only our own design files and documentation.
# Anything copyrighted by a third party, personal, secret or regenerable stays out.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Third-party copyrighted material (legal) — never publish
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendor datasheets, app notes, reference manuals and standards.
# Keep only our own index (datasheets/README.md) with links to the sources.
*.pdf
!docs/**/*_own.pdf
!docs/schematic/*.pdf
datasheets/**
!datasheets/
!datasheets/README.md
# Downloaded 3D models (vendor / EasyEDA / manufacturer licences vary).
# Models are referenced by path; each user fetches them (see README).
3d_models/**
!3d_models/
!3d_models/README.md
*.step
*.stp
*.wrl
*.STEP
*.STP
*.WRL
# Standards and paid documents, if ever placed in the tree
standards/

# Private agent runbook (owner's own, not part of the published project)
BRAHMASTRA.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Secrets and credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
credentials*
*token*.txt
# BQ76952 unseal / full-access keys and production OTP images with keys
*.keys
*_keys.*
otp_images/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Personal, OS and editor files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.lnk
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. KiCad local / generated files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.kicad_prl
fp-info-cache
*.lck
~*.lck
_autosave-*
*-backups/
.history/
*.bak
*-bak
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*-save.kicad_pcb
*-save.kicad_sch
*.tmp
# Exported netlists, reports and renders (regenerate with tools/ and kicad-cli)
*.net
*.rpt
erc*.json
drc*.json
/output/
/drc_reports/
/erc_reports/
/renders/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Note: project design rules (*.kicad_dru) ARE tracked — they are part of the design.
# Note: fabrication outputs go to production/ and are committed only for a released revision.
